 * Introduction:

  FPOFR is a Online File Request utility for CNet v3.05c. 

  It allows the users to upload a file request list to the BBS, and then the
  FPOFR pfile will find and mark the files for the user. No need to enter XX
  subdirs to get the files!! Now Finding/Marking/Downloading is EASY :))

  Here's the HELP file for OFR. So you can see how the format looks like.
 
                         ---- SYSTEXT:HELP/OFR ----

Command:        OFR
Purpose:        To upload a OFR Online File Request file
Available at:   All command prompts

A OFR Online File Request file is a text file which contain a number of lines
in the following format:

<Area Name>|<File Name>
<Area Name>|<File Name>
etc.       ^
etc.       `-> 'PIPE Char'

<Area Name> is the name you see when you do a [L]ist in the File Area.

<File Name> is the name of the file you want to request.

On this BBS your OFR file MUST be named: "<Your BBS>.OFR"


Entering OFR will begin the process of uploading your OFR Request file.
Once you enter OFR you will be asked if you wish to use your default transfer
protocol.  Select the protocol you wish to use.  The system will then ask you
to begin sending the OFR file or abort.  Press Return to upload the file, or
A to abort.

Once you have successfully uploaded a OFR file, the system will then start
marking your requested file(s), and show the name, area and status of each
request.



 * Requirements:

  CNET BBS v3.05c by Perspective Software.
  The C= Delete command.
  & AREXX  :^)


 * Installation:


  1) Create a dir in PFiles:, called FPOFR

  2) Copy the OFR.RMS, OFR.TXT into the PFiles:FPOFR/ directory.
     Copy the Help file OFR into your SysText:Help/ directory.

  Then add this line to your BBSMENU, under '2; Available everywhere'

       OFR    `5-   | #4PFiles:FPOFR/OFR.RMS %23}
 

 * Known Bugs:

  Subboards that contains MCI codes in the Subboard titles, won't be processed
  unless the user uses MCI codes in his .OFR file..

